From: Jason Rhinelander <jason@imaginary.ca>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:54:33 -0300
Subject: Allow 1.25.0 when building deb

We ship a 1.25.0+stf backport with the needed patch applied, so it is
fine and we can drop the stock package's 1.26.0 requirement.  (This is
coupled with a >= 1.25.0+stf requirement in debian/control).
---
 src/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 4d12419..805015a 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ configure_file(version.cpp.in version.cpp @ONLY)
 # 1.26.0 stops a server keeping a path's max UDP payload size when the client's IP address changes,
 # which stalls the connection when the new path's MTU is smaller.  session-deps' 1.25.0 carries that
 # fix as a patch.
-session_dep(libngtcp2 1.26.0 WITH libngtcp2_crypto_gnutls)
+session_dep(libngtcp2 1.25.0 WITH libngtcp2_crypto_gnutls)
 session_dep(gnutls 3.7.2)
 session_dep(nettle 3.5)
 session_dep(libevent_core 2.1 WITH libevent_pthreads)
